{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will set My face against that man.</b> If it was in secret. And some say its meaning is to cut off his seed." "<b>To defile My sanctuary.</b> For it is within the land of Israel." "<b>And to profane My holy name.</b> So that the nations will hear." "And it appears to us that the meaning of באבן שם המין (by the stone, the name of the species) is like ויהי לי שור וחמור (and I had ox and donkey), and the words of tradition are correct and they are truth. And Rabbi Jonah the Spanish grammarian, of blessed memory, said that the meaning of ובמשפחתו is: the one resembling him, and who brought us into this trouble? Only the plain meaning, for the common people will close their eyes because they are of his family."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {3 "The phrase באבן שם המין is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. נ״ע expanded to 'of blessed memory.' The trailing argument referencing Rabbi Jonah appears to jump between unrelated scriptural phrases (possibly from Lev. 20 and elsewhere), which may reflect a textual difficulty or a compressed multi-topic discussion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:20.283275407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}